  "raw_text": "45\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\n5\n):\n \nTrai kaiks s\ní\nlaba nani sut (b\nî\nla p\nî\nska bani\n \nulban ba) pain aisi kaikaia.\n \n–\n \nTry to read every syllable correctly.\n \n/\n\nIntenta leer cada sílaba correctamente.\n)\n\nBîla prahni ra\n \n–\n \nin short, in summary\n \n/ en resumen\n\nBîla prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto silence, to hush\n \n/ callar\n\nBîla sauhaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto swear, to curse, to say bad words\n \n/ jurar, maldecir, decir malas palabras\n\nBîla tânka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndefinition\n \n/ definición\n\nBîla\n \ntringsar\n \n(\nth\n-\n5\n)\n \n–\n \nstrange word, unknown word\n \n/ palabra extraña, palabra desconocida\n\nBîla twatwilkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nmessenger, someone who\n \ncarries a message\n \n/ mensajero, alguien que lleva\n\nun mensaje\n\nB\nî\nla walaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto obey\n, to listen to the word of\n, to heed\n \n/ obedecer\n, escuchar la palabra de\n, prestar atención\n\n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nB\nî\nla\n \nwali daukaia\n,\n \nWali daukaia\n)\n\n(Construct:\n \nB\nî\nli\n \nwalaia\n \n–\n \nto obey me\n \n/ obedecerme\n;\n \nB\nî\nlam walaia\n \n–\n \nto obey you\n \n/ obedecerte\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh31\n):\n \nYang b\nî\nli walbia kaka, ...\n \n–\n \nIf (they) obey me, ...\n \n/ Si (ellos) me obedecen,\n \n…\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb16\n):\n \nRait (Job)\n \nbîla\nm walisa, ...\n \n–\n \nIt’s\n \ntrue, Job obeys you, ...\n \n/ Es verdad, Job te obedece\n,\n \n...\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n08/19\n):\n \nLawi ai daukisa taim\n \nwilinkira bîla walisna\n \nki?\n \n–\n \nWhen I am counseled, do I willingly obey?\n \n/ Cuando\n\nme aconsejan, ¿\no\nbedezco\n \nde buena gana\n?\n)\n\nB\nî\nla walaia l\nâ\nka\n \n(a/t:\n \nB\nî\nla walan l\nâ\nka\n,\n \nB\nî\nla walaia ba\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nobedience\n \n/ obediencia\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n07/21\n):\n \nG\nȃ\nd ra b\nî\nla walaia ba kupia wina balisa\n \n–\n \nObedience to God comes from the heart\n \n/ La\n\nobediencia a Dios viene del corazón\n)\n\nB\nî\nla walanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nobedience\n \n/ obediencia\n\nB\nî\nla walikira\n \n(\ngf\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nobedient\n \n/ obediente\n\nB\nî\nla wali daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto obey, to listen\n \nto\n \nthe word of to do\n \n/ obedecer, escuchar\n \nla palabra para\n \nhacer\n \n(\nSee\n\nalso/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nB\nî\nla\n \nwalaia\n \n/\n \nWali daukaia\n)\n\nB\nî\nla walras\n \nkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto\n \nnot\n \nobey\n, to be disobedient\n \n/ no obedecer, ser desobediente\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner\n\ntambién:\n \nB\nî\nla lulkaia\n \n–\n \nto disobey\n \n/ desobedecer\n)\n\nUpla b\nîla\n \nwawalra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nperson who listens, obedient person\n \n/ persona que escucha,\n\npersona obediente\n\nUpla b\nîla\n \nwawalras\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nperson who doesn’t\n \nlisten,\n \nd\nisobedient person\n \n/ persona que no escucha,\n\npersona desobediente\n\nB\nî\nla yahpira\n \n(\nAlt:\n \nB\nî\nla yahpa\n,\n \nB\nî\nla tara\n)\n \n–\n \nbig\n-\nmouthed\n \n/\n \ntapudo\n \n(used as an insult\n \n/\n \nusado como un insulto)\n\nB\nîla\ns\n \n(Bilas)\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nmute, dumb, speechless\n \n/\n \nm\nudo, tonto, sin palabras\n\nKakma bara b\nî\nla prakaika\n \n(\ntkl\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nmask, something to cover the nose and mouth\n \n/ mascarilla, algo para cubrir\n\nla nariz y la boca\n\nLâ\n \nbîla\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \ncommandment\n \n/ mandamiento\n\nLilia bîla yabaia\n \n(\ntk\nl) (v)\n \n–\n \nto give commendation\n \n/ dar encomio\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nBîla pain (nani) wiaia\n)\n\nMiskitu b\nî\nla\n \n–\n \nMiskito language\n \n/\n \nl\nenguaje\n \nM\niskito\n\nPrakaia b\nî\nla nani\n \n–\n \nconcluding comments in the Christian Life and Ministry meeting\n \n/ comentarios finales en la\n\nreunión de Vida\n \ny Ministerio\n \nCristian\nos\n\nPrakaia bîla nani ba pain kaia sa\n \n(\nth\n-\n20\n-\ntit\n)\n \n–\n \nEffective Conclusion\n \n/ Hacer una\n \nBuena conclu\nsión\n\nSain bîla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsign language\n \n/ lenguaje de señas\n\nTâ krikaia b\nî\nla nani\n \n–\n \nopening comments, opening words, introductory words\n \n/ comentarios iniciales, palabras\n\niniciales, palabras\n \nde introducci\nó\nn\n\nTwi bîla\n \n–\n \npath or way to a savannah, path or way to a field, path or way to a pasture\n \n/ camino a una sabana,\ncamino a un campo, camino a un pasto\n\nYapti bîla\n \n–\n \nmother-tongue\n \n/ lengua materna\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-09/20\n):\n \nG\nȃ\nd Kingka l\nȃ\nka sturka yamni ba ai yapti bîla kat walisa taim, upla nani ba nahki ai dara walisa?\n \n–\n\nHow do people feel when they hear the good news of the kingdom in their mother-tongue?\n \n/ ¿Cómo se sienten las\npersonas cuando escuchan las buenas nuevas del reino en su lengua materna?)\n\nBila\n \n–\n \nsaid\n \n/ dijo\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nBila\n \nis sometimes used as a verb. It appears that\n \ndb\n \nmany times uses this word to say “\nsaid\n”.\n \nExample at Luk 7:43\n \n–\n\nJisas bila:\n \n—\nMan kasak aisaram\n. Some\n \nmight argue that in these cases, it is saying “\nfrom the mouth of Jesus\n”. However, when\n \ndb\n\nsays\n \nmouth\n, it uses the circumflex (\nBîla\n)\n \nand in the cases where it is used as verb, there is no circumflex.\n \n/\n \nBila\n \na veces se usa\ncomo verbo.\n \nParece que\n \ndb\n \nmuchas veces usa esta palabra para decir \"dijo\". Ejemplo en Lucas 7:43\n \n-\n \nJisas bila:\n \n—\nMan kasak",
